%% Structure source for workload-cluster-provisioning-detailed.svg. Keep the two in sync.
%% The SVG numbers requests only; the 201 reply is unnumbered there.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Op as Operator (nvkectl or API)
    box Management cluster
        participant Ctl as NVKE controller (API, reconcilers)
        participant Tmp as Temporal (workflows)
        participant CAPI as CAPNICo (with Cluster API)
        participant Spire as SPIRE server
    end
    participant NICo as NICo (bare metal)
    participant Node as Workload node (nvke-agent)
    participant Cust as Customer (kubectl)

    Op->>Ctl: POST /api/clusters
    Ctl->>Ctl: store cluster, queue work
    Ctl-->>Op: 201 Provisioning
    Ctl--)Tmp: ProvisionCluster
    Tmp->>CAPI: Cluster, NicoCluster
    loop For each node
        Ctl--)Tmp: ProvisionNode
        Tmp->>CAPI: NicoMachine, Machine
        CAPI->>NICo: create instance
        NICo->>Node: boot node OS image
        Node->>Spire: attest with TPM
        Tmp->>Node: preflight, Open vSwitch
    end
    Tmp->>Node: kubeadm init, install CNI
    Tmp->>Tmp: cluster Provisioned
    Tmp->>Node: kubeadm join (other nodes)
    Ctl->>Node: fetch admin kubeconfig
    Ctl->>Ctl: store as Secret
    Op->>Ctl: get kubeconfig
    Op--)Cust: hand over kubeconfig
    Cust->>Node: kubectl
